WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:18.520
Beauty and the Beast by Jean-Marie LeCranz de Beaumont Copyright Black Cat Publishing

00:30.000 --> 00:35.000
Chapter 1. Beauty's Family

00:36.000 --> 00:40.950
A rich man lives in a big city near the sea.

00:41.000 --> 00:45.030
He has got three daughters and three sons.

00:45.080 --> 00:51.030
One daughter is called Beauty because she is very beautiful.

00:51.080 --> 00:56.000
The other two daughters are called Rosalind and Hortensia.

00:56.200 --> 00:59.450
They are lazy and unfriendly.

01:00.280 --> 01:02.450
They like going out and having fun.

01:03.400 --> 01:06.650
They both want to find a rich husband.

01:07.640 --> 01:11.180
They do not like beauty because she is beautiful.

01:12.320 --> 01:14.740
Beauty has got long red hair.

01:15.320 --> 01:17.400
She is kind and friendly.

01:18.240 --> 01:21.140
She likes staying at home and reading books.

01:21.720 --> 01:24.270
She also likes playing the piano.

01:25.320 --> 01:27.230
Beauty's father is a merchant.

01:28.280 --> 01:33.610
One day he loses all his money because his ship is lost at sea.

01:34.360 --> 01:37.800
My dear children. He says sadly.
 
01:38.160 --> 01:40.000
I haven't got much money.

01:40.120 --> 01:41.770
We're poor.

01:42.720 --> 01:47.150
We must leave this big house and go and live in the country.

01:48.000 --> 01:51.700
Oh dear. Say the two sisters.
  
01:52.240 --> 01:55.710
We are poor. This is terrible.
 
01:56.560 --> 02:01.000
What bad luck. Say the three brothers.
 
02:01.200 --> 02:05.790
We have to work now. Says Beauty's father.
  
02:06.440 --> 02:09.790
Work. Say the two sisters.
  
02:10.760 --> 02:13.730
No. We don't want to work.
 
02:13.880 --> 02:16.530
And we don't want to live in the country.

02:17.320 --> 02:22.500
They start to cry.

02:23.000 --> 02:28.400
Beauty is sad but she says let's not cry.

02:28.450 --> 02:31.700
We can work and be happy without money.

02:31.900 --> 02:36.930
The family goes to the country and lives in a small house.

02:37.080 --> 02:42.440
Beauty gets up at four o'clock every morning to clean the house and cook.

02:42.540 --> 02:46.020
Then she washes the family's clothes in the river.

02:46.200 --> 02:49.500
The three brothers work in the country.

02:49.640 --> 02:53.090
Rosalind and Hortensia do not work.

02:53.140 --> 02:55.670
They do nothing all day.

02:55.720 --> 03:00.590
They sleep all morning and walk in the woods in the afternoon.

03:01.000 --> 03:04.470
I'm unhappy. Says Rosalind.
 
03:04.520 --> 03:08.950
I don't like the country because there's nothing to do.

03:09.060 --> 03:15.760
We can't go to the theatre and wear nice clothes. Says Hortensia.

03:15.820 --> 03:19.720
And we haven't got any friends.

03:19.820 --> 03:23.850
Look at Beauty. Says Rosalind angrily.
 
03:23.900 --> 03:28.570
She works and she's happy in this terrible place.

03:28.720 --> 03:32.670
Beauty's father says. Dear Beauty.
 
03:32.720 --> 03:36.460
You work a lot and you're always happy.

03:36.700 --> 03:38.910
You're a wonderful daughter.

03:43.000 --> 03:49.100
Listening activity. Here is an example.

03:49.220 --> 03:53.300
What does Rosalind want to buy for the summer?

03:53.420 --> 03:57.350
I want to buy a new red hat for the summer.

03:57.420 --> 04:01.000
But you have already got a pink one.

04:01.200 --> 04:05.720
What about a nice blue hat? No. I like red.
 
04:06.720 --> 04:08.670
One.

04:08.720 --> 04:13.670
Which shop is next to Marie's hat shop?

04:13.720 --> 04:18.670
Well, let's go to Marie's hat shop.

04:18.720 --> 04:21.670
Is the shop near the park?

04:21.720 --> 04:25.290
No. It's next to the bakery.
 
04:25.400 --> 04:29.670
Oh, I remember. Opposite the library.
 
04:29.720 --> 04:31.000
Two.

04:32.220 --> 04:35.870
What does Rosalind want to buy at the bakery?

04:35.920 --> 04:45.740
Oh, good. Then we can buy some chocolate biscuits at the bakery. I love them. Me too.
 
04:45.820 --> 04:50.150
I like chocolate cake and chocolate biscuits.

04:50.320 --> 04:53.670
Do we need to get some bread too?

04:53.720 --> 04:57.900
I don't think so. There is lots of bread at home.
 
04:59.720 --> 05:00.670
Three.

05:01.020 --> 05:05.570
What time does Marie's hat shop open on Saturdays?

05:05.820 --> 05:10.170
What time does the hat shop open?

05:10.200 --> 05:17.770
It usually opens at nine, but today is Saturday and it opens at half past nine.

05:18.020 --> 05:21.570
We must wait for fifteen minutes then.

05:21.720 --> 05:24.500
Four.

05:25.020 --> 05:30.670
What does Hortensia want to buy for the party?

05:30.720 --> 05:33.670
Let's put our coats on and go.

05:33.720 --> 05:35.070
Okay.

05:35.320 --> 05:41.670
Today I want to buy some new white shoes to wear with my white dress for the party.

05:41.720 --> 05:46.700
But you have already got nine pairs of white shoes.

05:50.720 --> 05:54.870
Chapter two. Beauty's Rose.
  
05:55.020 --> 06:01.100
A year later, Beauty's father gets an important letter.

06:01.220 --> 06:04.670
He calls his six children and says,

06:04.720 --> 06:07.670
Listen to this letter.

06:07.720 --> 06:09.670
Your ship is here.

06:09.720 --> 06:11.970
It is not lost at sea.

06:12.020 --> 06:14.170
Please come to the port.

06:14.220 --> 06:16.270
Everyone is happy.

06:17.020 --> 06:21.670
This is wonderful news. Say the three sons.
 
06:21.720 --> 06:24.500
Yes. Says their father.
 
06:24.620 --> 06:28.670
The ship with my goods is in the port.

06:28.720 --> 06:32.100
We're rich again. Says Rosalind.
 
06:32.320 --> 06:34.670
We can buy beautiful clothes.

06:34.720 --> 06:41.670
We can go back to our big house in the city. Says Hortensia.
 
06:41.720 --> 06:46.720
I must go to the port today. Says her father happily.
 
06:46.820 --> 06:51.670
Oh father. Says Hortensia.
  
06:51.720 --> 06:56.670
Bring me some new clothes and new hats.

06:56.720 --> 06:58.870
Yes. Says Rosalind.
 
06:58.920 --> 07:02.670
And some new shoes and jewels.

07:02.720 --> 07:05.670
Beauty's father looks at her and says,

07:05.720 --> 07:07.940
What do you want, Beauty?

07:08.020 --> 07:12.670
Please, don't spend your money, Father. Says Beauty.
 
07:12.720 --> 07:15.670
Just bring me a rose.

07:15.720 --> 07:20.070
Beauty's father gets to the port and finds his ship.

07:20.120 --> 07:22.670
But there are no goods on it.

07:22.720 --> 07:24.670
It is empty.

07:24.720 --> 07:28.670
What bad luck! He says angrily.
 
07:28.720 --> 07:33.670
I must go home and tell the children the bad news.

07:33.720 --> 07:37.670
On the way home he crosses a big forest.

07:37.720 --> 07:40.670
It is snowing and windy.

07:40.720 --> 07:42.200
He is lost.

07:42.300 --> 07:44.670
Where am I? He thinks.
 
07:44.720 --> 07:46.200
Where can I go?

07:46.420 --> 07:49.000
I'm very cold and tired.

07:49.120 --> 07:52.670
He hears some wolves and he is afraid.

07:52.720 --> 07:56.670
Suddenly he sees a big castle in the forest.

07:56.720 --> 07:58.970
And there are lights in the windows.

07:59.120 --> 08:01.670
Oh good. He thinks.
  
08:01.720 --> 08:05.670
Perhaps the people in the castle can help me.

08:05.720 --> 08:09.670
He takes his horse to the stable near the castle.

08:09.720 --> 08:13.970
He knocks on the big door of the castle but no one answers.

08:14.000 --> 08:16.670
He waits outside the door.

08:16.720 --> 08:21.670
Then he opens the door and goes inside.

08:21.720 --> 08:24.670
He sees a big hall with a fireplace.

08:24.720 --> 08:28.670
There is a long table with a lot of food on it.

08:28.720 --> 08:33.670
He is cold and sits near the fireplace.

08:33.720 --> 08:36.670
How strange! He thinks.
 
08:36.720 --> 08:38.770
There's no one here.

08:39.020 --> 08:44.670
He is hungry and sits down at the table and starts to eat.

08:44.720 --> 08:46.670
Then he is sleepy.

08:46.720 --> 08:51.670
He finds a warm, comfortable bed and falls asleep.

08:51.720 --> 08:56.670
The next morning he finds some new clothes near his bed.

08:56.720 --> 09:01.670
How nice. New clothes. He thinks.
  
09:01.720 --> 09:05.670
A kind person lives in this castle.

09:05.720 --> 09:09.220
He looks out of the window and is surprised.

09:09.320 --> 09:15.000
It's not snowing and it's a beautiful day. He thinks.
 
09:15.120 --> 09:17.800
And there are flowers in the garden.

09:17.900 --> 09:21.440
He gets dressed and goes to the hall.

09:21.620 --> 09:25.670
There are biscuits, chocolate and milk on the long table.

09:25.720 --> 09:27.670
He sits down and says.

09:27.720 --> 09:31.000
Thank you for this lovely breakfast.

09:31.100 --> 09:34.000
He looks round but sees no one.

09:34.100 --> 09:37.670
He eats and decides to go home.

09:37.720 --> 09:40.670
He goes to the stable and gets his horse.

09:40.720 --> 09:44.670
In the garden he sees some roses.

09:44.720 --> 09:47.670
Beauty wants a rose. He thinks.
 
09:47.720 --> 09:50.670
He takes a lovely one.

09:50.720 --> 09:53.720
Suddenly he hears a terrible noise.

09:57.720 --> 10:02.720
He turns round and sees an ugly monster.

10:05.720 --> 10:08.670
Listening activity.

10:08.720 --> 10:10.670
Here is an example.

10:10.720 --> 10:15.670
Where does beauty's father's ship come from?

10:15.720 --> 10:17.370
Good morning.

10:17.420 --> 10:20.670
Can you help me? I'm looking for my ship.

10:20.720 --> 10:24.670
There are eleven ships in the port this morning.

10:24.720 --> 10:26.670
What's the name of the ship?

10:26.720 --> 10:28.460
I don't know.

10:28.720 --> 10:31.670
It's a big ship and it comes from Italy.

10:31.720 --> 10:34.200
There are two big ships in the port.

10:34.400 --> 10:37.670
One from England and another from Turkey.

10:37.720 --> 10:42.670
No. My ship is from Italy.

10:42.720 --> 10:47.670
One. What is the ship like?

10:47.720 --> 10:51.670
Oh, perhaps you're looking for the blue one.

10:51.720 --> 10:56.670
No. The ship is red and black. Now I remember.
 
10:56.720 --> 11:01.670
It's near the black ship from Turkey.

11:01.720 --> 11:05.670
Two. Who is the captain of the ship?

11:05.720 --> 11:09.970
Good. Who is the captain of the ship?

11:10.020 --> 11:15.670
I don't know his name, but he is a young man with brown hair.

11:15.720 --> 11:20.670
Does he wear glasses? Yes, he does.
 
11:20.720 --> 11:22.670
Three.

11:22.720 --> 11:26.670
What time does the captain go to his ship?

11:26.720 --> 11:30.150
What time does he usually come here?

11:30.220 --> 11:36.670
He usually comes very early, at half past six in the morning,

11:36.720 --> 11:38.830
and he goes to his office.

11:38.920 --> 11:43.670
Then, at eight o'clock, he goes to his ship.

11:45.020 --> 11:49.970
Four. How does he usually travel to work?

11:51.720 --> 11:54.670
Does he ride his horse to work in the morning?

11:54.720 --> 11:58.670
Well, he usually comes by boat.

11:58.720 --> 12:03.670
He sometimes comes here on foot in summer.

12:03.720 --> 12:06.720
Thank you.

12:09.720 --> 12:14.670
Castle's. What is a castle?
 
12:14.720 --> 12:19.670
A castle is the home of a king or a very rich family.

12:19.720 --> 12:23.670
It protects the people who live there.

12:23.720 --> 12:31.670
Castle's have got high walls and small windows, so they are difficult to attack.

12:31.720 --> 12:40.670
Castle's are usually near rivers, near the sea, on hills or on mountains.

12:40.720 --> 12:44.670
History of castles.

12:44.720 --> 12:50.670
In the 10th century, people build small wooden castles in Europe.

12:51.720 --> 12:56.670
In 1066, William the Conqueror attacks England.

12:56.720 --> 13:00.670
He is from Normandy in France.

13:00.720 --> 13:05.670
He builds the first big stone castles in England.

13:05.720 --> 13:11.670
He builds the Tower of London in about 1078.

13:11.720 --> 13:17.670
The Normans build about 80 stone castles in England.

13:17.720 --> 13:24.000
There are a lot of stone castles in Europe in the 12th and 13th centuries.

13:24.620 --> 13:28.670
They are big, and they can protect a lot of people.

13:28.720 --> 13:33.670
Let's look at some important castles in Europe.

13:33.720 --> 13:38.670
Bodeum Castle, East Sussex, England.

13:38.720 --> 13:46.720
This is an old medieval castle with big square walls and a moat around it.

13:47.720 --> 13:50.670
Clams Castle, Scotland.

13:50.720 --> 13:57.670
This big castle has got a long history of ghosts and terrible secrets.

13:58.220 --> 14:02.670
It has got more than 100 rooms.

14:02.720 --> 14:06.670
Shenonso Castle, France.

14:06.720 --> 14:12.670
Shenonso Castle is on the Cher River in the famous Loire Valley.

14:12.720 --> 14:18.670
There are a lot of beautiful castles in this valley.

14:18.720 --> 14:22.670
Neuschwanstein Castle, Germany.

14:22.720 --> 14:27.670
This castle is like a picture in a fairy tale book.

14:27.720 --> 14:37.670
King Ludwig II built it in 1869 as his home.

14:37.720 --> 14:42.670
Chapter 3, The Beast.

14:42.720 --> 14:47.500
You're a bad man. Crys the Beast angrily.
 
14:47.720 --> 14:52.670
You come to my castle and I save your life.

14:52.720 --> 14:55.670
You eat here and you sleep here.

14:55.720 --> 14:59.670
And then you take one of my beautiful roses.

14:59.720 --> 15:02.670
For this you must die.

15:02.720 --> 15:08.670
Beauty's father starts to cry. Oh, sir, I'm sorry.
 
15:08.720 --> 15:10.670
You're very kind.

15:10.720 --> 15:13.090
Please don't be angry with me.

15:13.120 --> 15:16.670
This rose is for one of my daughters.

15:16.720 --> 15:21.670
My name is not, sir. It is Beast.
 
15:21.720 --> 15:24.670
Please call me by my name.

15:24.720 --> 15:27.670
You talk about your daughters.

15:27.720 --> 15:31.670
Then one of your daughters must die in your place.

15:31.720 --> 15:35.030
Oh no! There's Beauty's father.
 
15:35.120 --> 15:38.210
They're young and they don't want to die.

15:38.320 --> 15:42.700
Then you must come back here and die. Says the Beast.
 
15:42.820 --> 15:45.700
I can wait three months.

15:45.800 --> 15:48.100
Do you agree to come back?

15:48.200 --> 15:51.670
Beauty's father agrees to come back.

15:51.700 --> 15:54.670
My daughters must not die. He thinks.
 
15:54.700 --> 15:59.500
I want to go home and see my children for the last time.

15:59.600 --> 16:05.100
Before Beauty's father leaves the castle, the Beast talks to him.

16:05.200 --> 16:09.400
I'm not bad. Says the Beast.
  
16:10.410 --> 16:12.100
Go back to your bedroom.

16:12.200 --> 16:15.100
There is a big chest there.

16:15.200 --> 16:20.100
Fill it with everything you want. And it is yours.
   
16:21.620 --> 16:25.100
Beauty's father fills the chest with a lot of gold.

16:25.200 --> 16:28.670
Then he gets on his horse and goes home.

16:28.720 --> 16:32.670
When he is at home, he gives the rose to Beauty.

16:32.720 --> 16:37.140
Take this rose, Beauty. He says sadly.
 
16:37.720 --> 16:41.670
Let me tell you about my terrible adventure.

16:41.720 --> 16:48.670
He tells his children about the empty ship in the port, the castle in the forest and the Beast.

16:49.000 --> 16:52.670
Rosalind and Hortensia are angry with Beauty.

16:52.720 --> 16:54.300
They say...

16:54.720 --> 16:59.670
Father must die because you like roses. Beauty.
 
16:59.720 --> 17:02.200
No. Says Beauty.
 
17:02.300 --> 17:04.670
Father is not going to die.

17:04.720 --> 17:07.670
I'm going to the Beast's castle.

17:07.720 --> 17:11.670
No, dear sister. Say her three brothers.
 
17:11.720 --> 17:15.670
We are going to his castle and we're going to kill him.

17:15.720 --> 17:19.670
No. That's not possible. Says their father.
 
17:19.720 --> 17:22.670
The Beast is very big and strong.

17:22.720 --> 17:26.670
I'm old. I must go and die.

17:26.720 --> 17:29.670
But Beauty does not agree.

17:29.720 --> 17:33.670
She decides to go to the Beast's castle.

17:33.720 --> 17:39.670
No father. She says. You must not go. I want to go.
 
17:39.720 --> 17:43.000
Never my dear Beauty. Says her father.
 
17:43.100 --> 17:46.050
I'm not afraid. Says Beauty.
 
17:46.200 --> 17:49.900
You must live and look after my brothers and sisters.

17:50.000 --> 17:51.670
They need you.

17:51.720 --> 17:54.670
Beauty's father thinks for a moment.

17:54.720 --> 17:57.670
Then he says sadly.

17:57.720 --> 18:01.670
All right, Beauty. You can go.
 
18:01.720 --> 18:05.350
Beauty's brothers are very sad.

18:05.500 --> 18:08.670
But Hortensia and Rosalind are not.

18:08.720 --> 18:13.670
The next morning, Beauty and her father go to the Beast's castle.

18:13.720 --> 18:19.720
Inside the castle, they see a long table with a lot of good food on it.

18:20.720 --> 18:25.670
Beauty and her father are not hungry, but they sit down and eat.

18:25.720 --> 18:28.720
Suddenly, they hear a loud noise.

18:32.720 --> 18:36.430 
What's that terrible noise? Asks Beauty.
 
18:36.500 --> 18:39.670
The Beast is coming. Says her father.
 
18:39.720 --> 18:44.720
Beauty sees the Beast's ugly face and she is terrified.

18:45.000 --> 18:49.670
Oh, this Beast is really terrible, she thinks.

18:49.720 --> 18:55.670
The Beast looks at her and says. You're a brave girl.
 
18:55.720 --> 18:59.670
I'm very sorry about the rose from your garden.

18:59.720 --> 19:02.670
Says Beauty quietly.

19:02.720 --> 19:06.300
The Beast looks at Beauty's father and says. 

19:06.400 --> 19:09.670
You must go away tomorrow.
 
19:09.720 --> 19:15.670
And don't come back. Do you understand?
 
19:15.720 --> 19:20.200
Beauty's father looks at the Beast and then at his daughter.

19:20.300 --> 19:22.670
Oh, Beauty. He says.
 
19:22.720 --> 19:26.670
Please go home. Let me stay here.
  
19:26.720 --> 19:29.500
No, Father. Says Beauty.

19:29.600 --> 19:31.000
We must be brave.

19:31.100 --> 19:33.000
We're both tired.

19:33.100 --> 19:35.000
Let's go and sleep now.

19:35.100 --> 19:39.720
Tomorrow morning, you can go home to my brothers and sisters.

19:39.900 --> 19:42.950
That night, Beauty has a dream.

19:43.000 --> 19:46.670
In her dream, a good fairy says.

19:46.720 --> 19:49.200
You're a good girl, Beauty.

19:49.300 --> 19:51.670
And you've got a kind heart.

19:51.720 --> 19:54.670
You want to save your father's life.

19:54.720 --> 19:57.720
You're going to be very happy one day.

20:02.720 --> 20:07.670
Chapter 4. Life at the Castle.
  
20:07.720 --> 20:12.370
The next morning, Beauty's father leaves the castle.

20:12.420 --> 20:17.100
He is crying. Don't cry, Father. Says Beauty.
 
20:17.200 --> 20:19.670
Remember, I love you.

20:19.720 --> 20:24.670
Goodbye. Dear Beauty. Says her father.
 
20:24.720 --> 20:30.670
Beauty is terrified. The Beast is going to eat me tonight. She thinks.
 
20:30.720 --> 20:33.670
I want to enjoy my last day.

20:33.720 --> 20:36.670
I'm going to visit the garden of the castle.

20:36.800 --> 20:41.670
She goes to see the big garden and she is surprised.

20:41.720 --> 20:45.670
It is a beautiful garden with a lot of lovely flowers.

20:45.720 --> 20:48.670
Then she goes to see the big castle.

20:48.720 --> 20:51.670
She looks in all the rooms.

20:51.720 --> 20:54.670
On one door, she sees this sign.

20:54.720 --> 20:56.670
Beauty's room.

20:56.720 --> 21:00.200
She opens the door and sees a lovely room.

21:00.520 --> 21:04.670
There is a nice bed and a mirror on the wall.

21:04.720 --> 21:06.950
Beauty looks round and thinks.

21:07.000 --> 21:10.670
There's a piano and a lot of books for me.

21:10.720 --> 21:15.670
How strange. Perhaps the Beast doesn't want to eat me tonight.
 
21:15.720 --> 21:19.200
She takes a book and starts to read it.

21:19.400 --> 21:23.000
Suddenly, she sees these words on the pages.

21:23.100 --> 21:27.670
Welcome, Beauty. Don't be afraid.
  
21:27.720 --> 21:29.670
You're the Queen here.

21:29.720 --> 21:32.670
Tell me everything you want.

21:32.720 --> 21:37.670
I only want to see my poor father. Says Beauty.
 
21:37.720 --> 21:44.670
Suddenly, she sees her father in the mirror on the wall. He is very sad.
 
21:44.720 --> 21:49.670
She also sees her home and Hortensia and Rosalind.

21:49.720 --> 21:52.670
They are happy without beauty.

21:52.720 --> 21:56.300
The Beast is kind to me. She thinks.
 
21:56.500 --> 21:58.670
Why am I afraid of him?

21:58.720 --> 22:01.670
At twelve o'clock, she has lunch.

22:01.720 --> 22:04.670
After lunch, she goes to her room.

22:04.720 --> 22:08.670
What a beautiful piano. thinks Beauty.
 
22:08.720 --> 22:10.670
I want to play it.

22:10.720 --> 22:14.670
She plays some wonderful music on the piano.

22:14.720 --> 22:17.900
Then she looks at all the books in her room.

22:18.000 --> 22:22.140
Some of them have got pictures and others have not.

22:22.300 --> 22:27.670
She takes a book about flowers and looks at the pictures of different flowers.

22:27.720 --> 22:31.670
Then she sees pictures of roses of all colors.

22:31.720 --> 22:37.870
Now I want to go to the garden and look at the lovely roses. She thinks.
 
22:38.320 --> 22:42.670
She goes to the garden and stays there all afternoon.

22:42.720 --> 22:46.670
She looks at the flowers and feels happy.

22:46.720 --> 22:53.400
At dinner time, she sits down at the long table and then she hears the Beast coming.

22:53.520 --> 22:55.470
She is terrified.

22:56.320 --> 23:02.670
Beauty, can I sit here with you? Asks the Beast.
 
23:02.720 --> 23:06.670
You're the Lord of the Castle, says Beauty.

23:06.720 --> 23:11.670
And you're the Queen. Says the Beast.
  
23:11.720 --> 23:14.150
Can I ask you a question?

23:14.40 --> 23:18.320
Yes, of course. Says Beauty quietly.
  
23:18.50 --> 23:25.050
Am I very ugly? Asks the Beast.
  
23:25.120 --> 23:27.670
Beauty does not know what to say.

23:27.720 --> 23:30.670
She looks at him and thinks for a moment.

23:30.720 --> 23:34.670
Well, yes, you are. Says Beauty.
 
23:34.720 --> 23:37.100
But you're kind and polite.

23:37.220 --> 23:40.670
The Beast looks at Beauty and smiles.

23:40.720 --> 23:42.670
You're right.

23:42.720 --> 23:47.670
I'm terribly ugly, but I'm kind.

23:47.720 --> 23:50.670
This is your home now, Beauty.

23:50.720 --> 23:53.000
Please don't be sad.

23:53.100 --> 23:57.970
Some men are handsome, but they're not kind. Says Beauty.
 
23:58.100 --> 24:01.670
I prefer you because you've got a good heart.

24:01.720 --> 24:05.670
Thank you, Beauty. Says the Beast.
 
24:05.720 --> 24:11.670
Now Beauty is not afraid of the Beast and she eats a big dinner.

24:11.720 --> 24:15.670
The Beast looks at her and asks a question.

24:15.720 --> 24:19.070
Do you want to marry me, Beauty?

24:19.220 --> 24:23.670
What a question. Beauty is terrified.
 
24:23.720 --> 24:27.000
What can I say? Thanks, Beauty.
 
24:27.220 --> 24:31.670
She is silent for a moment and then she says...

24:31.720 --> 24:36.670
No, I'm sorry, I don't want to marry you.

24:36.720 --> 24:40.670
The Beast is angry and Beauty is afraid.

24:40.720 --> 24:43.670
Then he goes out of the room and says...

24:43.720 --> 24:46.720
Goodbye, Beauty.

24:51.720 --> 24:55.670
Chapter 5, The Magic Ring.

24:55.720 --> 25:00.670
Beauty spends three months at the beautiful castle.

25:00.720 --> 25:03.670
Every day she reads books and plays the piano.

25:03.720 --> 25:06.900
She walks everywhere in the big garden.

25:07.220 --> 25:12.670
She likes the tall trees and the flowers of different colours.

25:12.720 --> 25:16.670
She puts beautiful flowers in the rooms of the castle.

25:16.720 --> 25:20.670
Sometimes she makes perfume from the flowers.

25:20.720 --> 25:25.670
But the days are long and she is often lonely.

25:25.720 --> 25:30.670
Beauty often thinks about her father, her sisters and her brothers.

25:30.720 --> 25:33.670
I want to see my father again.

25:33.720 --> 25:35.670
She thinks sadly.

25:35.720 --> 25:39.670
And I want to see my home again too.

25:39.720 --> 25:45.670
The Beast goes to see her every evening at dinner time at 9 o'clock.

25:45.720 --> 25:49.670
They talk about interesting things and are happy together.

25:49.720 --> 25:53.670
Beauty is not afraid of his ugly face now.

25:53.720 --> 25:58.670
Every evening the Beast asks Beauty the same question.

25:58.720 --> 26:03.670
Beauty, do you want to marry me?

26:03.720 --> 26:08.670
And every evening Beauty answers... No.
 
26:08.720 --> 26:10.670
One day Beauty says...

26:10.720 --> 26:14.170
Why do you ask me the same question every evening?

26:14.320 --> 26:19.680
Because I hope to hear a different answer. Says the Beast.
  
26:19.820 --> 26:24.750
I'm sorry, I don't want to marry you. Says Beauty.
  
26:24.820 --> 26:27.700
The Beast is very sad.

26:27.820 --> 26:32.900
But I'm always going to be your friend. She says...
 
26:33.020 --> 26:37.670
You're a wonderful friend. Says the Beast.
 
26:37.720 --> 26:42.000
And you are too. Says Beauty, smiling.
 
26:42.10 --> 26:46.670
I know I'm terribly ugly. Says the Beast.
 
26:46.720 --> 26:48.670
But I love you a lot.

26:48.720 --> 26:53.500
I'm very happy with you. Please, don't leave me.
 
26:53.600 --> 27:00.000
Beauty's face becomes red and she is quiet for a moment.

27:00.220 --> 27:03.670
In the mirror of my room. Says Beauty.
 
27:03.720 --> 27:05.670
I see my poor father.

27:05.720 --> 27:08.000
He's sad and lonely.

27:08.120 --> 27:10.100
He thinks I'm dead.

27:10.200 --> 27:13.700
My sisters are married and my brothers are away.

27:13.800 --> 27:17.370
I want to see my father for the last time.

27:17.420 --> 27:19.900
Can I go and see him please?

27:20.000 --> 27:25.800
Yes. You can go and see your father. Says the Beast.
   
27:25.900 --> 27:29.900
But I'm going to be very sad without you.

27:30.100 --> 27:33.500
Oh, thank you. Says Beauty happily.
 
27:33.700 --> 27:36.000
Please don't be sad Beast.

27:36.100 --> 27:38.400
I'm going to come back in a week.

27:38.500 --> 27:41.300
All right. Says the Beast.

27:41.400 --> 27:47.670
You can visit your father tomorrow morning. But remember, you must come back in a week.
 
27:47.820 --> 27:53.000
Before you come back, put this ring on a table near your bed.

27:53.100 --> 27:58.670
It's a magic ring. Goodbye, Beauty.
 
28:01.720 --> 28:03.800
Flowers.

28:05.720 --> 28:10.670
There are about 200,000 different kinds of flowers in the world.

28:10.720 --> 28:17.670
Some are very small and others are very big, like the giant rufflesia.

28:17.720 --> 28:21.670
Let's look at some of these flowers.

28:21.720 --> 28:24.870
Flowers that grow in the desert.

28:25.720 --> 28:28.070
Some flowers grow in the desert.

28:28.320 --> 28:32.670
They need hot weather, but they do not need much water.

28:32.720 --> 28:41.670
Some of these flowers are the Apache plume, the desert lily, the yukka, and the prickly pear.

28:41.720 --> 28:44.670
Flowers that grow on water.

28:44.720 --> 28:51.670
Flowers like the lotus, the water lily, and the Louisiana iris grow in water.

28:51.720 --> 28:54.670
These flowers need very warm weather.

28:54.720 --> 28:58.670
You can see them in ponds and lakes.

28:58.720 --> 29:01.670
Tropical flowers.

29:01.720 --> 29:08.370
There are hundreds of beautiful tropical flowers in Hawaii and in the islands of the South Pacific.

29:08.420 --> 29:11.670
Hawaiian orchids are famous everywhere.

29:11.720 --> 29:14.400
Hawaiians make lays.

29:14.500 --> 29:16.670
They are colorful flower necklaces.

29:16.720 --> 29:20.300
They wear them and give them to tourists.

29:21.720 --> 29:24.670
Flowers as decorations.

29:24.720 --> 29:31.670
People use flowers as decorations for festivities like birthdays and weddings.

29:31.720 --> 29:38.670
On St. Valentine's Day, the favorite flower is the red rose.

29:38.720 --> 29:42.670
Flowers in art.

29:42.720 --> 29:46.670
Flowers are the favorite subject of a lot of painters.

29:46.720 --> 29:51.670
Van Gogh, Monet, and Suzanne, all paint flowers.

29:51.720 --> 29:58.670
Van Gogh is famous for sunflowers, and Monet is famous for water lilies.

29:58.720 --> 30:01.670
Flowers we can eat.

30:01.720 --> 30:04.670
Did you know that you can eat flowers?

30:04.720 --> 30:08.200
Some of the vegetables we eat are flowers.

30:08.300 --> 30:13.670
Broccoli, cauliflowers, and artichokes are flower vegetables.

30:13.720 --> 30:18.670
In Japan, people like eating cherry blossom soup.

30:18.720 --> 30:25.670
Some people make tea with rose petals, and others put them in salads.

30:25.720 --> 30:28.670
Flowers and perfumes.

30:28.720 --> 30:40.770
People make wonderful perfumes with flowers like roses, jasmine, violets, lilacs, orange blossoms, red tulips and peonies.

30:43.720 --> 30:49.670
Chapter 6, The Sisters Plan

30:49.720 --> 30:55.670
The next morning, Beauty wakes up in her bedroom in her father's house.

30:55.720 --> 30:58.670
She gets up and goes downstairs.

30:58.720 --> 31:01.670
When her father sees her, he cries.

31:01.720 --> 31:05.670
Beauty, is that you? How wonderful.
 
31:05.720 --> 31:08.200
My daughter is well and she's here.

31:08.300 --> 31:11.670
Beauty is very happy and hugs her father.

31:11.720 --> 31:17.670
Get dressed quickly and then tell me about the Beast. Says her father happily.
  
31:17.720 --> 31:23.670
She goes to her room and finds a chest full of beautiful clothes.

31:23.720 --> 31:28.400
This is a present from the Beast. Says Beauty to her father.
 
31:28.500 --> 31:32.670
He's very nice and gives me presents every day.

31:32.720 --> 31:35.670
She chooses some lovely clothes.

31:35.720 --> 31:40.000
I want to give these lovely clothes to Rosalind and Hortensia.

31:40.100 --> 31:45.300
She says, when she says this, the chest disappears.

31:45.400 --> 31:49.670
The Beast is watching you. Says Beauty's father.
 
31:49.720 --> 31:54.200
These beautiful clothes are for you and not for your sisters.

31:54.300 --> 31:57.670
Suddenly, the chest comes back again.

31:57.720 --> 32:02.670
That morning, Rosalind and Hortensia come to visit their sister.

32:02.720 --> 32:05.670
They are both very unhappy.

32:05.720 --> 32:10.670
Oh, Beauty. Says Rosalind. I'm unhappy.
 
32:10.720 --> 32:14.000
Why are you unhappy Rosalind? Asks Beauty.
 
32:14.100 --> 32:18.250
Oh, it's a long story. Says Rosalind.
 
32:18.400 --> 32:20.670
Please tell me. Says Beauty.
 
32:20.720 --> 32:26.100
My husband is handsome and he spends all day in front of a mirror.

32:26.200 --> 32:29.670
He never looks at me or talks to me.

32:29.720 --> 32:34.000
Oh dear, that's a big problem. Says Beauty.
 
32:34.100 --> 32:39.670
Hortensia says, My husband is very clever.
 
32:39.720 --> 32:43.400
But he doesn't like anyone and no one likes him.

32:43.620 --> 32:49.670
I can never invite my friends to lunch or dinner because he doesn't like them.

32:49.720 --> 32:54.670
We've got a lot of problems with our husbands. They say.
 
32:54.720 --> 32:57.670
My poor sisters. Says Beauty.
 
32:57.720 --> 32:59.670
I'm very sorry.

32:59.720 --> 33:03.900
Tell us about the Beast. Says Hortensia.
 
33:04.000 --> 33:09.670
Oh, the Beast is not a bad man. Says Beauty. He's very kind.
  
33:09.720 --> 33:13.670
I live in his beautiful castle and I'm the queen.

33:13.720 --> 33:16.500
I don't work. I read.
 
33:16.700 --> 33:19.670
Play the piano and walk in the garden.

33:19.720 --> 33:25.670
Every evening the Beast comes to see me at dinner and we talk about a lot of things.

33:25.720 --> 33:27.670
It's wonderful.

33:27.720 --> 33:32.670
The two sisters are very angry and they go to the garden.

33:32.720 --> 33:37.670
Beauty wears lovely clothes and shoes. Says Rosalind.
 
33:37.720 --> 33:41.200
She's like a queen. She's very happy.
 
33:41.420 --> 33:45.670
Why is she lucky and why are we unlucky?

33:45.720 --> 33:49.670
You're right Rosalind, says Hortensia.

33:49.720 --> 33:55.200
We are not very lucky. But maybe we can be lucky.
 
33:55.300 --> 34:02.300
Beauty has to return to the Beast in a week or he's going to get angry and eat her.

34:02.400 --> 34:05.670
Then we must keep her here. Says Rosalind.
 
34:05.720 --> 34:08.670
Then the Beast is going to get angry.

34:08.720 --> 34:13.100
During the week the two sisters are kind to beauty.

34:13.300 --> 34:15.400
They talk and laugh with her.

34:15.500 --> 34:17.670
They walk together in the country.

34:17.720 --> 34:20.670
Beauty is happy with her sisters.

34:20.720 --> 34:24.200
Rosalind and Hortensia love me. Beauty thinks.
 
34:24.500 --> 34:27.800
They're good sisters and I love them a lot.

34:27.900 --> 34:32.300
At the end of the week beauty says.

34:32.400 --> 34:35.200
I must go back to the Beast's castle.

34:35.320 --> 34:41.100
But her sisters start to cry. Oh, oh, Beauty. Says Rosalind.
 
34:41.400 --> 34:45.400
Please stay with us another week. We need you.
 
34:45.620 --> 34:48.970
Yes Beauty. Says Hortensia.
  
34:49.120 --> 34:50.970
Please don't leave us.

34:51.050 --> 34:54.670
We have fun with you and we love you.

34:54.720 --> 34:57.000
Yes. Says Rosalind.
  
34:57.050 --> 34:58.500
Stay with us.

34:58.600 --> 35:01.670
We can do a lot of things together.

35:01.720 --> 35:04.670
Beauty does not know what to do.

35:04.720 --> 35:08.720
She decides to stay another week.

35:11.720 --> 35:14.670
Chapter seven. The dream.

35:14.720 --> 35:20.700
The Beast is going to be very sad without me. Beauty thinks.
 
35:20.780 --> 35:24.670
But I want to stay with my family for a few more days.

35:24.720 --> 35:27.670
Then I'm going to go back to him.

35:27.720 --> 35:31.670
Beauty thinks about the Beast. She misses him.
 
35:31.720 --> 35:36.670
Ten days later beauty dreams about the Beast.

35:36.720 --> 35:41.000
In her dream the Beast is on the grass in the garden of the castle.

35:41.100 --> 35:42.670
And he's going to die.

35:42.720 --> 35:46.670
Beauty. Wispers the Beast.
 
35:46.720 --> 35:51.400
Today is the tenth day and you're not here.

35:51.500 --> 35:53.670
I can't live without you.

35:53.720 --> 35:56.670
I can't eat or drink.

35:57.520 --> 35:59.970
Beauty wakes up and thinks.

36:00.120 --> 36:03.670
The poor Beast is going to die without me.

36:03.720 --> 36:05.670
I must go back to him.

36:05.720 --> 36:10.670
She takes the ring and puts it on a table near her bed.

36:10.720 --> 36:15.670
The Beast is ugly but he's very kind. She thinks.
 
36:15.720 --> 36:17.670
Why don't I marry him?

36:17.720 --> 36:19.670
I'm happy with him.

36:19.720 --> 36:24.720
My sisters have handsome clever husbands but they're not happy.

36:25.720 --> 36:31.670
Beauty falls asleep and the next morning she wakes up at the Beast's castle.

36:31.720 --> 36:37.670
Today I'm going to wear a beautiful dress. Beauty thinks.
 
36:37.720 --> 36:42.670
At nine o'clock in the evening she goes to dinner and waits for the Beast.

36:42.720 --> 36:45.350
But he doesn't come to see her.

36:45.520 --> 36:48.300
What's happening? Beauty thinks.
  
36:48.400 --> 36:49.670
Where's the Beast? 

36:49.770 --> 36:55.200
Why isn't he here? Beast! She cries. 

36:55.250 --> 36:59.800
Beast! Where are you? Answer me!
 
37:00.720 --> 37:05.350
She opens the doors of all the rooms and looks everywhere in the castle.

37:05.450 --> 37:07.670
But she cannot find him.

37:07.720 --> 37:10.170
Suddenly she remembers her dream.

37:10.320 --> 37:14.670
She runs to the garden and sees the Beast on the grass.

37:14.920 --> 37:18.170
Oh no! She cries. Is he dead?
 
37:18.720 --> 37:22.000
She listens to his heart and it is beating.

37:22.200 --> 37:25.050
Good. He's not dead. She thinks.
 
37:25.100 --> 37:29.270
She gets some cold water from the river and wets his face.

37:29.320 --> 37:32.900
The Beast slowly opens his eyes.

37:33.000 --> 37:36.670
Beauty. He whispers.
 
37:36.720 --> 37:42.670
I'm dying. But I'm happy. Because you're here.
  
37:42.720 --> 37:46.670
No Beast! Crys beauty. Don't die.
 
37:46.720 --> 37:49.670
You must live and become my husband.

37:49.720 --> 37:53.720
I love you and I can't live without you.

37:56.720 --> 38:00.670
Chapter 8. The Prince.
 
38:00.720 --> 38:05.670
Suddenly all the lights of the castle and the garden turn on.

38:05.720 --> 38:08.670
There are beautiful fireworks in the sky.

38:08.720 --> 38:12.670
Beauty is surprised and looks at the castle.

38:12.720 --> 38:15.670
Then she turns round and looks at the Beast.

38:15.720 --> 38:17.670
What a surprise!

38:17.720 --> 38:20.670
She sees a handsome young man.

38:20.720 --> 38:24.670
Thank you beauty. Says the young man.
 
38:24.720 --> 38:27.170
The spell is broken.

38:27.250 --> 38:30.670
But where is the Beast? Asks beauty.
 
38:30.720 --> 38:34.670
I am the Beast. Says the prince.
 
38:34.720 --> 38:39.290
I don't understand. Says beauty. Who are you?
  
38:39.400 --> 38:44.400
I'm a prince. And this is my castle. Says the young man.
  
38:44.720 --> 38:49.400
Sometimes a bad witch puts a spell on a prince.

38:49.500 --> 38:52.670
And only true love can break the spell.

38:52.720 --> 38:55.670
Now I know your love is true.

38:55.720 --> 38:59.670
The prince takes her hand and says.

38:59.720 --> 39:02.670
Do you want to marry me beauty?

39:02.720 --> 39:08.670
Beauty looks at the handsome prince and says. Yes I do.
 
39:08.720 --> 39:12.000
Beauty and the prince go to the castle.

39:12.100 --> 39:15.670
When she opens the door she is surprised.

39:15.720 --> 39:20.670
My family. You're all here. Christ beauty.
 
39:20.720 --> 39:23.670
She is happy when she sees her family.

39:23.720 --> 39:26.670
They talk and laugh together.

39:26.720 --> 39:30.270
Suddenly she sees the good fairy from her dream.

39:30.320 --> 39:33.200
Beauty. Says the good fairy.
 
39:33.320 --> 39:35.500
You've got a kind heart.

39:35.600 --> 39:40.670
And you're going to marry the prince and become a princess.

39:40.720 --> 39:44.300
Then the good fairy looks at beauty's two sisters.

39:44.400 --> 39:49.300
You're both bad, lazy and unkind. Says the fairy.
 
39:49.420 --> 39:51.800
You don't love anyone.

39:51.900 --> 39:54.670
The fairy says some magic words.

39:54.720 --> 39:58.720
And suddenly Rosalind and Hortensia become statues.

39:59.720 --> 40:01.400
Oh no. Christ beauty.
 
40:01.620 --> 40:04.100
My sisters are statues.

40:04.400 --> 40:08.670
Your sisters have got hearts of stone. Says the fairy.
 
40:08.720 --> 40:11.000
Now they can't move.

40:11.100 --> 40:13.670
But they can see and hear everything.

40:13.720 --> 40:20.700
When they understand their mistakes they can become Rosalind and Hortensia again.

40:21.720 --> 40:25.170
The next day beauty and the prince get married.

40:25.220 --> 40:28.670
Everyone dances and sings in the castle.

40:28.720 --> 40:30.670
It is a happy day.

40:30.720 --> 40:34.670
People give flowers to beauty and the prince.

40:34.720 --> 40:38.670
The prince sees tears in beauty's eyes and says...

40:38.720 --> 40:41.300
Don't cry my beauty.

40:41.400 --> 40:44.720
We are going to be very happy together.
